<title>FRANCE: French October unemployment falls 12,000.</title>
<headline>French October unemployment falls 12,000.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The seasonally adjusted number of people unemployed in France in October fell by 12,000, or 0.4 percent, to 3,100,800, the Labour Ministry said.</p>
<p>The jobless rate, based on International Labour Organisation (ILO) criteria, which exclude jobseekers who did any work, was unchanged at 12.6 percent.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-Oct   month-on-month year-on-year</p>
<p> Unemployment		3,100,800    -0.4 pct	   +5.3 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		  170,700    -3.9 pct	   +1.8 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations 376,500    -1.4 pct	   +1.2 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits    353,300    +1.3 pct	   +0.7 pct</p>
<p> Men under 25		  290,900    -1.3 pct	  +7.5 pct</p>
<p> Women under 25		330,500     0.0 pct	  +3.4 pct</p>
<p> Men between 25 and 49   1,041,000    -0.3 pct	  +6.6 pct</p>
<p> Women between 25 and 49 1,065,300    -0.3 pct	  +3.0 pct</p>
<p> Men 50 and over	     213,700    -0.2 pct	  +8.5 pct</p>
<p> Women 50 and over	   159,400    -0.5 pct	  +9.2 pct</p>
<p> Forced redundancy	    29,986	NA		+6.9 pct</p>
<p> Jobless for over 12 mos 1,062,200     0.4 pct	  +1.6 pct</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
